Covers rscd-server, rscd-community-client, rscd-www and rscd-api.

The project carries no third-party jars. Connector/J was replaced by
server/util/sql/MysqlClient, MINA by server/util/net, and XStream by
XmlObjects on both sides, so nothing in the build inherits an obligation
from a dependency.

rscd-www-deprecated/ is the old PunBB site. It is not covered here and is
not going into the repository.


LINEAGE

RSCD descends from RSCDaemon, a RuneScape Classic server begun in 2006-2007
by eXemplar, SeanWT, Philodespotos and Mediator, and continued by Reines,
who brought it to the stable release the community ran. RSCDaemon
was worked on in the open and shared as a community project throughout;
its source went fully public after the project ended, and most later RSC
servers -- RSCEmulation among them -- start from that code.

No licence text was ever attached to it. That is recorded here as fact,
not as a claim about anyone's intent: the code was released to the
community to be used and built on, and this is that use. Attribution to
the authors above stays in this file permanently, and it travels with any
fork of this repository.

What arrived from upstream is the engine skeleton -- the packet loop, the
tile and pathing model, the persistence and entity-definition layer -- as
recovered by decompilation from the released build. Everything a player
touches was written here: the 50 quests, all 18 skills, the minigames, the
combat and drop tables, the world data rebuilt from the genuine Jagex
cache, the community world list, the client's script tiers. RSCDaemon's
authors built an engine to Jagex's blueprint and stopped well short of the
game; the game is ours.

The tree has also moved off the JDK 8 it was stuck on. The internals it
reached through are gone -- sun.reflect.ReflectionFactory by way of
XStream, MINA, the applet and AWT assumptions -- and it builds and runs on
current JDKs.

